PanVK (Mesa 26.2.6, MIT; Mesa's notices are kept as they are): two switches of the tiler heap, both off by default.

STARBITE_PANVK_PIPE=1: the batches take the two halves of the tiler heap in turn and name theirs in the submit's
requirements (bit 8 a half is named, bit 9 the second), so a kernel that knows the bits (bsd/dev/starlte_gpu.c sgu_pipe,
sgu_slots=2) may run a vertex/tiler chain beside the fragment chain of the batch before it.
STARBITE_PANVK_BINS=<hex mask>: only these levels of the tiler's bin hierarchy (and always the coarsest one Mesa chose).
Written on 12 November 2026 in a local tree (s9-night-ui); recorded here on 17 November from that tree, unchanged.

